Part of #186 and follow-up to #188.

Field evidence on 2026-09-05 showed a successful/accepted hotspot join followed seconds later by another setup attempt and selected-network release. This slice makes Android hotspot join ownership process-wide, matching the process-wide selected network it controls.

Changes:
- coalesce duplicate joins for the same credentials while the native request is in flight;
- suppress repeat joins for credentials that are already accepted/bound, including when a new Cubit/page instance is created;
- serialize a genuinely different invite behind the current request instead of racing two process-network selections;
- invalidate the lease on explicit leave or observed link loss so a real recovery can retry;
- add privacy-safe diagnostics without SSID/passphrase;
- add MethodChannel regression coverage for in-flight coalescing, stable post-connect suppression, and retry after explicit teardown.

This does not close #186: one-QR transport bootstrap, full stale-callback/epoch hardening, and repeated physical-device acceptance remain outstanding.

