The governed LMS SCORM staging harness used `GITHUB_RUN_ID` alone as its synthetic fixture marker. GitHub reruns reuse the same run ID while incrementing `GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT`, so a rerun after a partial/failed cleanup could recreate the same course titles, ZIP names, manifest identifiers and package version marker as the previous attempt.

This PR changes only the staging QA harness and its regression contract:
- fixture marker is now `run_id-run_attempt`, preventing collisions between reruns of the same workflow run;
- the marker remains propagated through synthetic course titles, ZIP names, SCORM manifest identifiers and completion-manifest package version;
- regression coverage locks the rerun-safe marker;
- regression coverage also locks the existing idempotent cleanup contract (`DELETE` 200/404 accepted, followed by required GET 404) and the workflow's `always()` cleanup step.

No product/runtime behavior, business semantics, frontend, Worker routes, schema/migrations, production data, production deployment, #265, or ANAC transmission is changed. Does not overlap open #326 (eDB lifecycle cleanup), #328 (MRO responsive staging coverage), or #331 (canonical final-record hashing foundation).

