## Root cause
Approved annotation mutations treated `NoteStore` boolean persistence failures as success. `setComment()` / `setName()` and struct-field `save()` can return `false`, while the executor continued to return `{ ok: true }`. `annotation.set-type` already failed closed on the same contract.

## Change
- reject `setComment(...) === false` with `AIError('tool_failed', ...)` before UI success publication;
- reject the initial `setName(...) === false` before the coupled symbol rename;
- treat a `false` return while restoring the prior name after a symbol-rename failure as rollback failure instead of silently claiming the rollback succeeded;
- reject `notes.save?.() === false` for struct-field persistence;
- preserve the existing successful mutation path and `annotation.set-type` fail-closed behavior.

No evidence/budget/cancellation contract, non-AI owner, threshold, denominator, corpus, or workflow is changed.

